varin@hardy.u.washington.edu (Byron Varin) writes:

>I was walking along and ran into a boulder.  I pushed it about 8 squares and 
>then it got stuck.  Is there a way to go further in that direction?

	Could be.  You may have pushed the boulder up against another
boulder, a secret door, or just a plain door that happened to be
closed.  If you want to try to go around the rock, drop *everything* -
including your armor - and try to squeeze through.  It's probably a
dead end, but maybe not.

>What does the doggie do?

	What do dogs normally do?  He (she?) will fight monsters and
can be trained to fetch stuff.  Just be sure to keep him well fed.
You can also start off with a cat, which does the same thing.

>I have read about shopping and paying the bills and stuff, but where are the 
>stores.  The game starts at level one.  I can't go up or I quit.  It seems all
>I can do is go down.  How far do you have to go?

	The stores usually start appearing on level 2 or 3.  Note
that with the exception of the recently added Gnome Town level, a
level will have at most one shop.  I have found stores as deep as 30th
level.

>How can I find out which mundane weapon is better than the other.  I know
>about the super weapons but what about katana vs. longsword vs. orcish dagger?

	Weapons are varied enough that it's best just to figure it out
on a case-by-case basis.  The only rule of thumb I would propose is
that blessed or enchanted weapons are usually better than uncursed
ones, and that cursed weapons should be avoided.

